  "purpose": "Bind the r=4 falsifier and the 27-draw RC-8 control by hash before review.",
  "SUMMARY_LINES_CHECKED_AGAINST_THE_ARTIFACT": "Every figure below was read from RESULTS.json, not from the producer's prose summary. Four Coordinator summary defects are recorded this session; CORR-20260803-c92db5 is the worst.",
  "outcomes": {
    "RANK_1_r4_falsifier": "DID NOT FIRE, outcome code C2. r=4 reads FULLY SATURATED: W>=1 on every one of 2^31 trials and every one of 2^30 in the paired arm, excess 1073741824 = 2^30, which is the ARITHMETIC CEILING of the statistic (rate 1.0 over a modeled null of 2^-30) and NOT an unbounded effect size. Pairing verified field by field -- sbox_spec, sbox_seed, amask, smask, trials, seed, arm_id, key_hex and thread_seeds all equal to BATCH-004's r=5 arm, with rounds the only difference. A reproduction control returned BATCH-005's D-AES-K1 EXACTLY: 14 hits, same whist, same W_ge1_by_word.",
    "WHAT_DID_DIE_IS_MY_QUEUE_S_PREMISE": "The BATCH-006 queue asserted the profile 'rises to a peak at r=5'. IT DOES NOT. The measured profile is MONOTONE DECREASING and saturated at r <= 4: r=2 2^30, r=3 2^30, r=4 2^30, r=5 13.5x, r=6 0.5x. r=5 is the LAST ROUND COUNT WITH A SUB-SATURATED ABOVE-NULL READING, not a peak. The monotone-decay language the campaign's artifacts actually use survives; the peak framing I introduced does not.",
    "RANK_2_RC8": "27 draws, all pinned (bijective, 5120 round-trips each, 0 failures), ZERO DEAD. 25 ALIVE and 2 INDETERMINATE under the strict BATCH-004 rule; 27/27 ALIVE under the BATCH-005 form. Lower bound on the preserving fraction: 0.7847 strict, 0.8950 not-DEAD, pooled with the 2 prior draws 0.7984 and 0.9019. AGAINST THE 0.224 IT REPLACES. The 0.90 target is met under the not-DEAD and BATCH-005 readings and NOT under the strict ALIVE reading; the producer reported both and correctly declined to choose, since which rule governs is a judgement about the frozen criterion.",
    "structural_anomaly": "At r <= 4, whist = [0,0,0,N,0]: W = 3 on EVERY trial, with W_ge1_by_word = [0, N, N, N]. Exactly three of four plaintext words are preserved deterministically and the one never preserved is word 0, the ACTIVE word. Recorded as an observation; no mechanism claimed. r=4 saturation is NOT AES-specific -- an arm under a drawn S-box saturates too."
  },
  "A_FIFTH_COORDINATOR_ABSENCE_DEFECT_FOUND_BY_THE_PRODUCER": {
    "what_I_asserted": "The BATCH-006 queue and task card state that the instrument has only ever run at r in {2,5,6,10} and that the low side of the profile has never been measured.",
    "what_is_true": "FALSE AS WORDED. r=3 and r=4 yoyo arms ALREADY EXIST in coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-001/tasks/yoyo5/analysis.json, measured 2026-08-02 on the AES-NI instrument at 2^32 and 2^33, both saturated, alongside r=5 at 16.75x/15.75x and r=6 at 0.75x.",
    "what_survives": "yoyo_sbox_v2 had only run at r in {5,6} and its predecessor at r in {2,5,6,10}; no r=4 arm was ever PAIRED to an r=5 arm or run under a drawn S-box. This task supplies both.",
    "how_it_was_found": "The producer applied CORR-20260803-c92db5's rule instead of repeating my claim: it searched (grep -rl W_ge1 over coordination, ledger, knowledge, docs, experiments -- 68 files, every rounds value tabulated) and DISCLOSED THE FINDING IN ITS PREREGISTRATION BEFORE MEASURING, so its confirmed prediction cannot be read as a lucky call.",
    "assessment": "This is the FIFTH instance this session of asserting the state of something without looking. It is the second of the CORR-20260803-c92db5 form -- a claimed absence -- and I inherited it from the BATCH-005 red team's enumeration and repeated it without redoing the search. In fairness to that red team, BATCH-001 was an explicit scratchpad with no ledger record. The rule held anyway: the producer named the paths it searched, and that is why its version is reliable."
  },
